WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.839
Over 30 years since Return of the Jedi, Harrison
Ford, Carrie Fisher, and Mark Hamill are back

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.559
with a new young cast to take us to a galaxy
far, far away.

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:15.780
I'm Jan and this is 15 things you probably
didn't know about Star Wars: The Force Awakens.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.730
The design of Kylo Ren's lightsaber was partly
inspired by a dinner party conversation between

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:25.810
director JJ Abrams and his friend Jonathan
Ive, who just happens to be Apple's Chief

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.810
Design Officer.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:32.070
Ive suggested the new lightsaber should be
less precise, more uneven or "spitty", as

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.080
he put it, and added that making it more "more
analogue and more primitive" would give it

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.020
a "more ominous" feel.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.370
Captain Phasma's shiny armoured costume was
actually originally pitched as a costume for

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.370
Kylo Ren.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.460
For story reasons, JJ Abrams decided it wouldn't
work for that character, but liked the design

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.790
so much that he decided it was perfect for
Captain Phasma.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:58.610
In fact, that silvery chrome-like design reminded
Abrams of a 1979 horror film in which the

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.080
antagonist attacks his victims with a silver
sphere.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.190
The name of that film was Phantasm, which
provided the inspiration for the name of Captain

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.190
Phasma.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.890
Oh, and by the way, according to screenwriter
Lawrence Kasdan, Captain Phasma was originally

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.550
going to be a male character but the role's
gender was later swapped and Gwendoline Christie

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.050
was cast.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:22.940
The hard, white plasticky look of Stormtroopers
made costume designer Michael Kaplan think

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.370
of his iPhone, which gave him the idea for
the sleek look of the Stormtrooper costumes

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.840
in The Force Awakens.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:34.000
The new Stormtrooper costumes are also tougher
and more flexible than the original vacuum-formed

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.630
suits as they were cast in a thicker polyurethane
plastic.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:45.280
Oscar Isaac's character Poe Dameron was partly
named after JJ Abrams' assistant at Bad Robot,

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.300
Morgan Dameron.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.890
However, Abrams can't quite remember the origins
of the character's first name, but thinks

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.700
it may have been subconsciously named after
his daughter's toy polar bear which is called

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.700
Po.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.031
As for the name BB-8, according to Abrams
both the letter B and the number 8 were just

00:02:00.031 --> 00:02:04.530
"sort of how [the droid] looked to [him]"
and he simply liked the onomatopoeic sound

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.130
of the name.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:12.110
Before going on set, to ready herself to play
Rey, Daisy Ridley would listen in her trailer

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.990
to I'll Make A Man Out Of You from Disney's
1998 animated feature Mulan.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:21.270
And that wasn't Ridley's only musical experience
while filming The Force Awakens.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:25.890
The young actress, who specialised in musical
theatre at Tring Park School for the Performing

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.250
Arts in the UK, says she couldn't stop singing
on set to the point that director JJ Abrams

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.569
actually bet her she couldn't make it a whole
day without bursting into song!

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:40.010
When he auditioned for the role of Finn in
The Force Awakens, John Boyega watched Mark

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:45.020
Hamill and Harrison Ford's original Star Wars
auditions on YouTube and drew inspiration

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.240
from approach to the material.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.190
Boyega's favourite character in all the Star
Wars movies is Han Solo because he relates

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:56.270
to Solo's attitude of 'just trying to make
some money and get by'.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:00.709
Carrie Fisher was not only told to lose weight
to play Princess Leia in the very first Star

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:05.730
Wars movie, despite only weighing 105 pounds
at the time, but Fisher says she also had

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.349
to lose over 35 pounds for The Force Awakens.

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:14.630
Mark Hamill also shed around 50 pounds to
return to the world of Star Wars.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:20.780
JJ Abrams brought Oscar-winning special effects
artist and animatronics wiz Neal Scanlan out

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:24.890
of retirement to bring to life the creatures
of The Force Awakens.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:30.020
Scanlan's team designed over 100 creatures,
using a mix of prosthetics and animatronics,

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.819
while some even had 5 or 6 people inside operating
them.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:38.550
The emphasis was on recreating the practical
feel of the creatures from the original trilogy,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:43.430
while making the best use of technological
advances like 3-D printing and small elements

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.569
of CGI to enhance the final look.

00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:52.090
As R2-D2 is such a fan favourite, it seems
fitting that The Force Awakens version of

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.709
everyone's favourite blue-and-white droid
was actually built by two Star Wars uber-fans!

00:03:56.709 --> 00:04:03.680
At the 2013 Star Wars Celebration in Germany,
Kathleen Kennedy was so impressed by the fully-functioning

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:08.390
R2-D2 replica made by Lee Towersey and Oliver
Steeples, who are British members of the R2

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.459
Builders Club, that she recommended them to
work on the movie!

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:15.930
The new R2-D2 the pair built for the film
is made of fibreglass and aluminium.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:21.609
So, you may know that the Millennium Falcon's
circular sensor dish was replaced with a rectangular

00:04:21.609 --> 00:04:26.789
one for The Force Awakens as the original
was lost when Lando flew the ship in Return

00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:27.789
of the Jedi.

00:04:27.789 --> 00:04:31.889
But the production designers also accommodated
a special request from Harrison Ford that

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:36.580
the dashboard switches on the new Falcon have
proper springs so they'd stay in place when

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.580
they were flipped.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.849
As a keen amateur pilot Ford was irritated
that the original Falcon's switches didn't

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:43.770
do that.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:48.789
Composer John Williams, who scored the original
Star Wars trilogy and the prequels, has likened

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:53.129
writing music for The Force Awakens to "adding
paragraphs to a letter that's been going on

00:04:53.129 --> 00:04:54.430
for a number of years."

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:58.189
However, Williams didn't consult his scores
for the previous films before starting work

00:04:58.189 --> 00:05:02.699
on his seventh Star Wars movie because, he
says, "it's a bit like riding a bike that

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:04.830
you haven't been on since you were ten years
old.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.900
You do remember."

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:12.289
After director JJ Abrams bumped into composer
Lin-Manuel Miranda at a performance of Miranda's

00:05:12.289 --> 00:05:17.639
hugely successful Broadway musical Hamilton,
Abrams asked him to compose music for a Cantina-style

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:19.259
scene in The Force Awakens.

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:23.629
However, Miranda didn't actually get to see
the scene he was scoring.

00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:27.819
Abrams just sent him the temporary music they'd
been using and Miranda took it from there,

00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:32.850
exchanging music files with Abrams over email
until the pair had completed the co-written

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:33.850
piece.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:39.319
Although a huge fan of the original Star Wars
trilogy, JJ Abrams very nearly turned down

00:05:39.319 --> 00:05:44.469
the opportunity to direct The Force Awakens
as, when producer Kathleen Kennedy first approached

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:48.639
him, he was still busy on post-production
for Star Trek Into Darkness and didn’t want

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:53.660
to take on another huge franchise especially
as he had plans for a 6-month family vacation.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.849
But when Kennedy told him he’d have a blank
canvas for the film, Abrams felt the chance

00:05:57.849 --> 00:06:01.140
to explore what had happened to Han, Leia
and Luke since we last saw them was just too

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.140
big to pass up.

